package ${BASE_PACKAGE}.feature.${FEATURE_NAME}

import ${BASE_PACKAGE}.domain.DomainError

/**
 * UI state for [${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}Screen]. Immutable; mutated only inside
 * [${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}ViewModel.container] via `intent { reduce { ... } }`.
 *
 * **No default values.** Every property is explicit so the call site states its
 * full intent and adding a field forces every constructor to be revisited. The
 * starting state lives in [Companion.Initial] (the single source of truth used by
 * the ViewModel's `container(...)` and by tests) — not as constructor defaults.
 *
 * **`internal`.** State never leaves the feature module. The feature's only public
 * surface is [${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}Route], its Koin module, and `add${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}Entries`
 * (see ${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}NavEntry.kt). See docs/architecture.md § Visibility.
 *
 * One-shot events (navigation, toasts, snackbars) live as **consumable state slots**
 * on this class — not as Orbit `SideEffect`s. UI observes the slot, consumes it,
 * then calls the matching `onXxxConsumed()` intent to clear it. See README and
 * docs/architecture.md for rationale.
 *
 * If state grows complex and a flat data class no longer fits (mutually-exclusive
 * sub-states, page-level transitions like Loading/Loaded/Error), prefer a
 * `sealed interface ${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}State` with `data object`/`data class`
 * children. Keep the flat shape when in doubt — easier to evolve.
 */
internal data class ${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}State(
    val loading: Boolean,
    // DomainError carried as-is; the UI maps it to a string resource at render time
    // (domain stays free of presentation strings — see docs/i18n-a11y.md).
    val error: DomainError?,

    // Consumable event slots — set inside intent {}, cleared by paired onXxxConsumed().
    val pendingMessage: String?,
) {
    companion object {
        /** Starting state. Used by the ViewModel's `container(...)` and by tests. */
        val Initial = ${FEATURE_NAME_PASCAL}State(
            loading = false,
            error = null,
            pendingMessage = null,
        )
    }
}

